 Git is a downloadable program that runs directly on your computer's operating system.

When u do git init, it will convert the normal file into a git repo 
An Ordinary Folder (The "Dumb" Folder)
• No Memory: If you rewrite a file, save it, and delete the old code, the old code is gone forever.
• No History: You can't see what the project looked like yesterday, last week, or two months ago.
• Messy Backups: If you want to save a working version, you have to manually duplicate the folder and name it something like my-project-v2, my-project-final, or my-project-FIXED.



